      {
        "id": "A1",
        "assertion": "Token discovery is platform-native: Linux discovery reads each candidate process environment from procfs instead of invoking ps, so the real-execution verification suites pass on the existing tests, while a synthetic procfs fixture proves the Linux branch selects exactly the token-carrying processes and an unreadable proc root still yields a cleanup failure instead of a passed check.",
